chowClass -- Finds the (fundamental) class of a subscheme in the Chow ring of the ambient space
***********************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        chowClass(IX)
        chowClass(IX,A)
  * Inputs:
      * IX, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, an ideal in the multi-graded
        coordinate ring of \PP^{n_1}x...x\PP^{n_m}; *note makeProductRing:
        makeProductRing, builds the graded coordinate ring of
        \PP^{n_1}x...x\PP^{n_m}.
      * A, a *note quotient ring: (Macaulay2Doc)QuotientRing,, the Chow ring of
        \PP^{n_1}x...x\PP^{n_m}. This ring can be built by applying *note
        makeChowRing: makeChowRing, to the coordinate ring of
        \PP^{n_1}x...x\PP^{n_m}.
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * Strategy (missing documentation) => ..., default value "multidegree",
        multidegree, using "prob" uses a probabilistic method which is
        sometimes faster on large examples
  * Outputs:
      * isMultHom, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, the class
        [X] in A where X is the subscheme associated to IX

Description
===========

Given a subscheme X of \PP^{n_1}x...x\PP^{n_m} this method computes [X] in the
Chow ring of \PP^{n_1}x...x\PP^{n_m}.

+--------------------------------------+
|i1 : R=makeProductRing({6})           |
|                                      |
|o1 = R                                |
|                                      |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                   |
+--------------------------------------+
|i2 : x=gens(R)                        |
|                                      |
|o2 = {a, b, c, d, e, f, g}            |
|                                      |
|o2 : List                             |
+--------------------------------------+
|i3 : J=ideal(x_0*x_2-x_4*x_5)         |
|                                      |
|o3 = ideal(a*c - e*f)                 |
|                                      |
|o3 : Ideal of R                       |
+--------------------------------------+
|i4 : clX=chowClass(J,Strategy=>"prob")|
|                                      |
|o4 = 2H                               |
|       1                              |
|                                      |
|     ZZ[H ]                           |
|         1                            |
|o4 : ------                           |
|        7                             |
|       H                              |
|        1                             |
+--------------------------------------+
|i5 : clX2=chowClass(J,ring(clX))      |
|                                      |
|o5 = 2H                               |
|       1                              |
|                                      |
|     ZZ[H ]                           |
|         1                            |
|o5 : ------                           |
|        7                             |
|       H                              |
|        1                             |
+--------------------------------------+
|i6 : clX==clX2                        |
|                                      |
|o6 = true                             |
+--------------------------------------+

