intersectionProduct -- A class in the Chow ring of the ambient space representing the Fulton-MacPherson intersection product of two schemes inside a variety
************************************************************************************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        intersectionProduct(IX,IV,IY)
        intersectionProduct(IX,IV,IY,A)
  * Inputs:
      * IX, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, a multi-homogeneous ideal
        defining a closed subscheme of \PP^{n_1}x...x\PP^{n_m}; *note
        makeProductRing: makeProductRing, builds the graded coordinate ring of
        \PP^{n_1}x...x\PP^{n_m}.
      * IV, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, a multi-homogeneous ideal
        defining a closed subscheme of \PP^{n_1}x...x\PP^{n_m}; *note
        makeProductRing: makeProductRing, builds the graded coordinate ring of
        \PP^{n_1}x...x\PP^{n_m}.
      * IY, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, a multi-homogeneous ideal
        defining a smooth complete intersection in \PP^{n_1}x...x\PP^{n_m};
        *note makeProductRing: makeProductRing, builds the graded coordinate
        ring of \PP^{n_1}x...x\PP^{n_m}.
      * A, a *note quotient ring: (Macaulay2Doc)QuotientRing,, the Chow ring of
        \PP^{n_1}x...x\PP^{n_m}. This ring can be built by applying *note
        makeChowRing: makeChowRing, to the coordinate ring of
        \PP^{n_1}x...x\PP^{n_m}.
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * Verbose (missing documentation) => a *note Boolean value:
        (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, default value false,
  * Outputs:
      * intProd, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, a class in
        the Chow ring A of \PP^{n_1}x...x\PP^{n_m} representing the
        Fulton-MacPherson intersection product of X with V in Y (where X is the
        scheme associated to IX, etc.).

Description
===========

For subschemes X,V of a smooth complete intersection subvariety Y of
\PP^{n_1}x...x\PP^{n_m} this command computes the Fulton-MacPherson
intersection product of X with V in Y as a class in the Chow ring of
\PP^{n_1}x...x\PP^{n_m}. Note that this command requires that Y is a smooth
complete intersection subvariety, however this is not checked internally.

+-----------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = makeProductRing({3})                  |
|                                               |
|o1 = R                                         |
|                                               |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                            |
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i2 : (x,y,z,w) = toSequence gens R             |
|                                               |
|o2 = (a, b, c, d)                              |
|                                               |
|o2 : Sequence                                  |
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i3 : Q = ideal(x*y-z*w)                        |
|                                               |
|o3 = ideal(a*b - c*d)                          |
|                                               |
|o3 : Ideal of R                                |
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i4 : L1 = ideal(x,w)                           |
|                                               |
|o4 = ideal (a, d)                              |
|                                               |
|o4 : Ideal of R                                |
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i5 : L2 = ideal(y,w)                           |
|                                               |
|o5 = ideal (b, d)                              |
|                                               |
|o5 : Ideal of R                                |
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i6 : intersectionProduct(L1,L2,Q,Verbose=>true)|
|      2 2                                      |
|[Y]= H H , alpha= 2H  + 2H                     |
|      1 2           1     2                    |
|                       3 3                     |
|Projective degrees= {7H H }                    |
|                       1 2                     |
|         3 3                                   |
|s(X,Y)= H H                                    |
|         1 2                                   |
|                              3                |
|Segre pullback to diagonal = H                 |
|                              1                |
|                2                              |
|Chern class = 2H  + 2H  + 1                    |
|                1     1                        |
|                                               |
|      3                                        |
|o6 = H                                         |
|      1                                        |
|                                               |
|     ZZ[H ]                                    |
|         1                                     |
|o6 : ------                                    |
|        4                                      |
|       H                                       |
|        1                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i7 : intersectionProduct(L1,L1,Q)              |
|                                               |
|o7 = 0                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------+

