isMultiHom -- Tests if an ideal is multi-homogeneous with respect to the grading of its ring
********************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        isMultiHom(X)
  * Inputs:
      * X, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, an ideal in the multi-graded
        coordinate ring of \PP^{n_1}x...x\PP^{n_m}; *note makeProductRing:
        makeProductRing, builds the graded coordinate ring of
        \PP^{n_1}x...x\PP^{n_m}.
  * Outputs:
      * isMultHom, a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, whether the
        input ideal is multi-homogeneous with respect to the grading of its
        ring

Description
===========

Given an ideal in the coordinate R ring of \PP^{n_1}x...x\PP^{n_m} this method
tests if whether the input ideal is multi-homogeneous with respect to the
grading on R.

+---------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = makeProductRing({1,2})                                |
|                                                               |
|o1 = R                                                         |
|                                                               |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                                            |
+---------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : x=gens R                                                  |
|                                                               |
|o2 = {a, b, c, d, e}                                           |
|                                                               |
|o2 : List                                                      |
+---------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : degrees R                                                 |
|                                                               |
|o3 = {{1, 0}, {1, 0}, {0, 1}, {0, 1}, {0, 1}}                  |
|                                                               |
|o3 : List                                                      |
+---------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : isMultiHom ideal(x_0^2*x_2+x_1*x_2^2)                     |
|Input term below is not homogeneous with respect to the grading|
| 2       2                                                     |
|a c + b*c                                                      |
|                                                               |
|o4 = false                                                     |
+---------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : isMultiHom ideal(x_0^2*x_2+x_1^2*x_3)                     |
|                                                               |
|o5 = true                                                      |
+---------------------------------------------------------------+

